.TH DISTRODECK 1 "2026-08-23" "distrodeck distrodeck 0.10.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
distrodeck \- Export and restore packages before distro upgrades.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B distrodeck
\fIcommand\fR [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
distrodeck exports installed packages and sources, then re-installs them after a distro upgrade.
.SH CONFIGURATION
distrodeck reads optional config files from \fI/etc/distrodeck/config.ini\fR and \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/distrodeck/config.ini\fR, or \fI~/.config/distrodeck/config.ini\fR when \fIXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR is unset.
.PP
The \fB[apt]\fR section can define \fIofficial_hosts_common\fR, \fIofficial_hosts_ubuntu\fR, \fIofficial_hosts_debian\fR, or distro-specific \fIofficial_hosts_<id>_override\fR entries as comma-separated host lists.
.PP
See \fIexamples/config.ini\fR for a sample configuration.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B export
Export installed packages and sources
.TP
.B diff
Compare an export file against the current system
.TP
.B import
Import packages and sources
.TP
.B self-update
(self-upgrade)
.TP
.B update
Update system packages
.TP
.B upgrade
Run distro upgrade
.TP
.B cleanup-kernels
Clean up old auto-installed kernels
.TP
.B security
Apply security upgrades
.TP
.B repo-repair
Repair apt repo issues
.TP
.B doctor
Check system prerequisites
.TP
.B install-tools
Install optional tools via a TUI checklist
.TP
.B git-status
Enable or disable git status in the shell prompt
.TP
.B git-aliases
Manage recommended git aliases
.TP
.B preflight
Run preflight checks
.TP
.B logs
View logs
.TP
.B clear-logs
Delete all logs
.TP
.B sysinfo
Show full system info
.TP
.B config-edit
Edit common system config files (TUI)
.TP
.B net-tools
Run installed network tools (TUI)
.SH COMMAND HELP
.SS export
.nf
usage: distrodeck export [-h] [--output OUTPUT]
                         [--appimage-dirs APPIMAGE_DIRS] [--include-config]
                         [--config-dirs CONFIG_DIRS]
                         [--config-exclude CONFIG_EXCLUDE]
                         [--config-archive CONFIG_ARCHIVE]
                         [--include-config-files]
                         [--config-files CONFIG_FILES] [--include-user-tools]
                         [--include-services]

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --output OUTPUT
  --appimage-dirs APPIMAGE_DIRS
  --include-config      Include system config snapshots (opt-in)
  --config-dirs CONFIG_DIRS
                        Colon-separated config dirs (default:
                        /etc:/etc/apt:/etc/dnf:/etc/pacman.d)
  --config-exclude CONFIG_EXCLUDE
                        Exclude patterns for config snapshot (repeatable)
  --config-archive CONFIG_ARCHIVE
                        Path for config snapshot archive
  --include-config-files
                        Include key config files as entries
  --config-files CONFIG_FILES
                        Colon-separated config files (default:
                        /etc/hosts:/etc/fstab:~/.ssh/config)
  --include-user-tools  Include user-level tools (pipx, npm, composer, nuget,
                        cargo, gem, go)
  --include-services    Include enabled/active systemd services
.fi
.SS diff
.nf
usage: distrodeck diff [-h] --input INPUT [--sections SECTIONS] [--detailed]
                       [--json] [--exit-code] [--appimage-dirs APPIMAGE_DIRS]

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --input INPUT         Export file to compare
  --sections SECTIONS   Comma-separated sections to compare (default: all
                        comparable sections; see --help for the list)
  --detailed            List the differing entries, not just the counts
  --json                Output a machine-readable JSON report
  --exit-code           Exit 1 when differences are found (0 when in sync)
  --appimage-dirs APPIMAGE_DIRS
.fi
.SS import
.nf
usage: distrodeck import [-h] --input INPUT [--apply] [--update-sources]
                         [--apply-config] [--config-archive CONFIG_ARCHIVE]
                         [--apply-services] [--apply-config-files]
                         [--sections SECTIONS] [--cleanup-extras]
                         [--appimage-dirs APPIMAGE_DIRS]

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --input INPUT
  --apply
  --update-sources
  --apply-config        Restore config snapshot from the export file
  --config-archive CONFIG_ARCHIVE
                        Override config snapshot archive path
  --apply-services      Enable systemd services captured in the export
  --apply-config-files  Restore exported config files to their paths
  --sections SECTIONS   Comma-separated sections to restore (e.g.,
                        apt_manual,snap,flatpak)
  --cleanup-extras      Remove snap/flatpak extras not present in the export
  --appimage-dirs APPIMAGE_DIRS
.fi
.SS self-update
.nf
usage: distrodeck self-update [-h]

options:
  -h, --help  show this help message and exit
.fi
.SS update
.nf
usage: distrodeck update [-h] [--cleanup-kernels]
                         [--keep-kernels KEEP_KERNELS]

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --cleanup-kernels     Clean up old auto-installed kernels after a successful
                        update
  --keep-kernels KEEP_KERNELS
                        Previous kernel versions to keep when --cleanup-
                        kernels is used
.fi
.SS upgrade
.nf
usage: distrodeck upgrade [-h] [--target-codename TARGET_CODENAME]
                          [--cleanup-kernels] [--keep-kernels KEEP_KERNELS]

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --target-codename TARGET_CODENAME
                        Target codename for Debian upgrades (or set
                        DISTRODECK_TARGET_CODENAME)
  --cleanup-kernels     Clean up old auto-installed kernels after a successful
                        distro upgrade
  --keep-kernels KEEP_KERNELS
                        Previous kernel versions to keep when --cleanup-
                        kernels is used
.fi
.SS cleanup-kernels
.nf
usage: distrodeck cleanup-kernels [-h] [--dry-run] [--keep KEEP]

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --dry-run             Preview kernel packages that would be removed
  --keep KEEP, --keep-kernels KEEP
                        Previous kernel versions to keep in addition to the
                        running kernel
.fi
